{
  "_about": "Every number in the explainer comes from here. All measured on one Apple M4 Pro (10 P + 4 E cores, 128-byte cache lines, 128 KB L1D per P-core, 16 MB L2 per cluster), macOS, rustc 1.98.0, bench profile (fat LTO), threads not pinned, 2026-10-09/10. Units: M records/s unless a key says ns or us. Pairs are two rounds in separate processes. 'one_line' = both cursors in one 128-byte line (ring at 0 mod 128); 'two_lines' = cursors on separate lines (ring at 64 mod 128). Rings heap-placed at a fixed offset for the two-thread cells unless 'stock_harness' is noted.",
